.page exec 1 replace the shell by a program

# SYNOPSIS
*exec* _COMMAND_ [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`exec` is a gapsh builtin. It starts _COMMAND_ in place of the shell: nothing comes back and the shell's process becomes the program. The program is looked up in `PATH`. Without a command `exec` does nothing.

# EXIT STATUS
127 if the program cannot be found, 126 if it cannot be run.

# EXAMPLES
    exec pnote /tmp/note.txt

# SEE ALSO
eval(1), command(1)
